{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"fa2661909c967e11a9a1d98f35ed98a0651b9c5c58d39a3b8afccbc4cbb3d991","digest":{"component_or_area":"tickets store fetch and initialization","key_entities":["actions/checkout","filter: blob:none","git clone","rebar init","init.py:375","worktree add --orphan","verify-identity","merge-base","reconcile-bridge.yml","gerrit-verify.yaml",".bridge_state","verify_authorship.py","derive_caused_by","resolve_event_commit","resolve_position_commit",".github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml",".github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml"],"problem_keywords":["git clone cost","partial clone","tickets store","CI performance","fail-open bootstrap","empty divergent store","blob:none filter"],"propositions":["Fresh full clone of tickets costs 1.04 GiB and 59s wall time; --filter=blob:none reduces to 68.7 MiB and 14.3s, a 15x improvement.","When tickets fetch times out in CI, rebar silently bootstraps a fresh empty orphan store, diverging from origin/tickets and causing all reads to return empty results.","Blob:none partial clone is safe for rebar's access patterns including verify-identity and commit-ancestry scoping because the complete commit graph is preserved while only blobs are lazy.","The fail-open orphan bootstrap must be replaced with fail-closed behavior that exits non-zero and creates no branch on fetch failure.","Partial clone filters must be inherited by subsequent manual worktree mounts and verified via actual byte measurements, not just config presence assertions."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787550047227010001,"uuid":"ad889c7b-b7cd-4888-8772-5840bd831ff8"}